{"ts":"2026-11-14T19:43:50.569Z","run_id":"telem_default-fb-06741-1f0476744ddf4b2e915cd845e25c90ce","question_id":"fb-06741","setup":"telem_default","seq":10,"type":"answer","data":{"final":"About 6.2%. Margins (operating income + cash flow statement D&A, divided by total revenues): FY2018 (20,437+10,529)/500,343 = 6.19%; FY2019 (21,957+10,678)/514,405 = 6.34%; FY2020 (20,568+10,987)/523,964 = 6.02%. The 3-year average is about 6.185%, which rounds to 6.2%. Sources: https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/104169/000010416920000011/R7.htm, https://www.smith-leonard.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/walmart-10-K.pdf","status":"ANSWERED","citations":["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/104169/000010416920000011/R7.htm","https://www.smith-leonard.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/walmart-10-K.pdf"],"searches":1}}
